In article <1pa8soINN7ts@matt.ksu.ksu.edu> thak@matt.ksu.ksu.edu (Charles C Mercer) writes:
>A few questions for you demigods out there...
>
>1) Praying: what does it do? Where? When? Why?
Praying asks for divine intervention.  You can get all of your ailments
cured or get your levels drained, depending on how pissed off your
god is as you.

Anywhere, Anytime, Everytime you're in trouble and need help.
>
>2) Where are these altars at? How exactly do you use them?

Altars are randomly located around dungeon.
You can sacrifice corpses at them to either convert the altar to your god
or if it's already your god's altar, improve your standing with your god
so that praying is more sucessful.  Sometimes you also get goodies from your
god.

Dropping items on an altar will let you know their blessed/cursed status.
>
>3) What's up with these tin things?

Ever been to Food Lion?  They are just tinned up food.  Stay's fresher that
way but hard to open.  You eat them just like corpses.
>
>4) Do corpses do anything for you? (I eat them, yes, but what do they do besides
>   fill you up?)

Keep you from starving.  Also eating some corpses gives you intrinsics.
Eg, eating a floating eye corpse, gives you See Invisible.
Sometimes it won't work

>
>5) What's this wishing stuff?
You can get wishes in the game.  This allows you to wish for any item.
There are limits.  I wouldn't try wishing for a +100 long sword if I were you.
>
>6) An incredibly general question: WHAT IS A FAQ? HOW DO I FIND THEM?

FAQ:  Frequently Asked Questions:  It's posted every two weeks (?) to the
newsgroup.  Keep your eyes open for it.
